# 2026-10-11: Adding vector types
#
# As with any other entity types, we need a record of the identifier(s), owner,
# stewards, etc., so SQLite tables are still used. However, in contrast to
# *currencies* where each variable instance is an *account*

# An *ivector* has a set of stewards (*primids*) and an owner (the *primid*
# that first created it). It also has a set of users. In contrast to the case
# of a *money" (where two *accounts* are adjusted simultaneously by the same
# scalar value), an *ivector* can only be adjusted/updated by one agent at a
# time.
#
# As with any other *currency* type, all changes are recorded in a journal
# identifying:
# - date & time
# - which agent updated the variable
# - the update (vector)
# - the value following the update (vector)
# - an annotation
#
# As with *currencies* of type "money", an error (or disputed update) can be
# reversed by a subsequent update.

